{
  "status": "recommended-semantic-bindings-not-an-installed-keymap",
  "mod": "Meta (the Mac Command key)",
  "defaults": {
    "terminalEditor": "nano",
    "browser": "Google Chrome",
    "terminal": "Kitty",
    "vimMode": false
  },
  "bindings": [
    {
      "chord": "Meta+Return",
      "action": "terminal.local.open"
    },
    {
      "chord": "Meta+Space",
      "action": "finder.toggle"
    },
    {
      "chord": "Meta+b",
      "action": "rail.toggle"
    },
    {
      "chord": "Meta+Left",
      "action": "focus.left"
    },
    {
      "chord": "Meta+Right",
      "action": "focus.right"
    },
    {
      "chord": "Meta+Up",
      "action": "focus.up"
    },
    {
      "chord": "Meta+Down",
      "action": "focus.down"
    },
    {
      "chord": "Meta+Shift+Left",
      "action": "window.move.left"
    },
    {
      "chord": "Meta+Shift+Right",
      "action": "window.move.right"
    },
    {
      "chord": "Meta+Shift+Up",
      "action": "window.move.up"
    },
    {
      "chord": "Meta+Shift+Down",
      "action": "window.move.down"
    },
    {
      "chord": "Meta+1..9",
      "action": "workspace.select"
    },
    {
      "chord": "Meta+Shift+1..9",
      "action": "window.move.workspace"
    },
    {
      "chord": "Meta+f",
      "action": "window.fullscreen.toggle"
    }
  ],
  "preserveApplicationBindings": [
    "Control+n",
    "Control+Shift+n",
    "Control+l",
    "Control+t",
    "Control+w",
    "Control+c",
    "Control+v",
    "Control+Shift+c",
    "Control+Shift+v"
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Bind with the installed public Domicile command helpers; validate normalized ownership with ownedChords.",
    "Read stock defaults at the pinned SDK: remove inherited h/j/k/l navigation and modal Vim modes instead of spreading DEFAULT_KEYBINDINGS blindly.",
    "Mouse, touchpad and application controls remain available; the tour never requires remembered chords.",
    "Do not reuse Tom\u2019s global Control+n launcher or his NAS terminal launcher for Tarek\u2019s standalone laptop."
  ]
}
